# gb10 container manifest — PINNED images for the on-demand compute stack.
#
# Reproducibility rule: pin by DIGEST, not just tag. The first time a container
# is created, resolve its digest on the box and paste it here:
#   docker inspect --format '{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' <image>
# gb10-serve.sh records the running image's digest to Postgres
# (run.container_image) so every run is traceable.
#
# These images + the HF cache volume are the ONLY heavy state we keep on the box.
# Containers are created once then docker stop/start-ed — never torn down.
#
# Per-model recipes live OUTSIDE this file. Serving is Docker-container-per-model
# (`swap-vllm-<served-name>` on :8002); the per-model serve recipe (SERVE_MODEL / SERVED_NAME /
# SERVE_CONTAINER / MAX_LEN / QUANT / REASONING_PARSER / SPEC_ARG / COMPILE_ARG / KV_ARG /
# EXTRA_ARGS + UI metadata) lives in the dedicated `gb10-model-configs` repo (models/<name>.env),
# which gb10-serve.sh sources via SERVE_ENV_FILE and the swap-ui parses directly. This file keeps
# only the SHARED stack: pinned images + digests, HF cache volume, ports, and reachability. The
# SERVE_MODEL / SERVED_NAME / SERVE_CONTAINER below are just the bare fallback defaults for a
# no-arg gb10-serve.sh run; the live values come from the model .env.

# --- Serve: vLLM with NVFP4 (NVIDIA DGX Spark path) ---
# vLLM 0.27.1 (upstream stable, NOT the NVIDIA nvcr image — see below). Verified clean on this box
# at the time of the 2026-08-12 bump (v0.25.1 -> v0.27.1, skipping v0.26.0 — no bump landed for
# it) against the then-canonical qwen36-27b-dense (nvidia/Qwen3.6-27B-NVFP4, ModelOpt NVFP4
# auto-detected quant): loaded clean, MTP(k=3) spec-decode + forced PIECEWISE cudagraph
# unaffected, tool-calling (qwen3_xml) still correct, bf16 KV cache still resolved explicit (not
# silently fp8). qwen36-27b-dense itself was removed 2026-09-02 (superseded as fallback default
# by Qwen3.8-27B-FP8, see below) — this paragraph is left as the historical record for why
# v0.27.1 is pinned, not a claim that the current default was tested this way.
#
# DROPPED the local logprob-clamp patch layer (manifests/vllm-logprob-clamp.Dockerfile, cherry-
# picking unmerged vLLM PR #48585) as part of this bump. PR #48585 is STILL unmerged upstream as of
# 2026-08-12, but the bug it worked around (logprobs coming back None/NaN/inf under our FP8-path
# quantization, crashing /v1/completions with "Out of range float values are not JSON compliant:
# nan") did NOT reproduce on bare v0.27.1: re-ran the exact original trigger (echo=True,
# logprobs=1) plus a harder stress variant (n=2, logprobs=5, longer prompt) — zero non-finite
# values either time. Something else in 0.26/0.27's numerics work likely fixed it incidentally.
# The Dockerfile is left in the repo (harmless, unused) in case this regresses on a future bump —
# don't delete it without re-confirming the bug is gone on whatever version you're checking.
# If it DOES resurface: rebuild with
#   docker build --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:<new-tag> -f manifests/vllm-logprob-clamp.Dockerfile -t vllm-openai-logprobclamp:<new-tag> .
# (the patch's exact-match asserts on vllm/logprobs.py and .../serving.py may need updating if
# those files were refactored since v0.25.1 — check the assert failures if the build errors out.)
# Bumped to v0.28.0 2026-09-02, hoping vLLM PR #51812 ("Align Qwen GDN gates with speculative
# tokens", merged 2026-08-11 -- just after v0.27.1 was cut, so first available here) would fix a
# logprob-correctness bug found on v0.27.1: MTP spec-decode (k=3) collapsed lm-eval-harness MMLU
# from ~0.84-0.89 (spec-decode off) to ~0.45 (spec-decode on) on the Qwen3.8-27B family (GDN
# hybrid-attention architecture), on both the unsloth NVFP4 and official FP8 checkpoints. IT DID
# NOT FIX IT: re-ran the identical test on v0.28.0 against qwen3.8-27b-fp8 -- MMLU 0.892 spec-
# decode off vs 0.362 spec-decode on, i.e. still broken (if anything slightly worse), with
# near-zero throughput benefit from spec-decode to show for it (24.6 vs 25.5 tok/s, 35.8%
# acceptance -- much lower than the ~60-69% seen on the NVFP4 checkpoint on v0.27.1). Root cause
# remains open. KEPT v0.28.0 anyway (sanity-passed clean with spec-decode off, matching the
# production qwen3.8-27b-fp8.env recipe which has SPEC_ARG/COMPILE_ARG explicitly cleared) since
# it's otherwise a superset of v0.27.1's fixes; the bare-fallback default's spec-decode-ON-by-
# default behavior (see gb10-serve.sh) is now confirmed hazardous on this box regardless of
# vLLM version -- do not rely on it for this model family without re-verifying logprob accuracy.
VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.28.0-aarch64
VLLM_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:2a7cde230b59f3ce6cab33dd245ba6bee41aa87b38c9fe84f966ff24016813ce

# WHY NOT the NVIDIA nvcr image: nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm lags upstream by 1-2 months and older builds
# carry a FULL-cudagraph/TurboQuant MTP corruption bug. Vanilla vllm/vllm-openai:v0.27.1-aarch64
# resolves it in combination with --compilation-config '{"cudagraph_mode":"PIECEWISE"}'.
# Entrypoint differs from the old nvcr image: pass `--model <repo>` directly as CMD args, NOT
# `vllm serve <repo>` (vllm-openai's entrypoint already IS the API server).

# Model weights: pre-download into HF_CACHE_VOL before serving (vLLM's lazy load
# stalls on first run). DISABLE Xet — the huggingface_hub Xet downloader hangs at
# 0% on this box; classic HTTP works:
#   docker run --rm -e HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1 -v tokenai-hf-cache:/root/.cache/huggingface \
#     vllm/vllm-openai:v0.24.0-aarch64 --model Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8
# (An HF_TOKEN lifts the ~10 MB/s unauthenticated rate limit.)
SERVE_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8
SERVED_NAME=qwen3.8-27b-fp8

# --- Train: ms-swift (ModelScope) — handles Qwen3.6 hybrid-MoE LoRA + merge ---
# Pin the ms-swift image tag the box pulls; deps are baked into the resident
# tokenai-train container, not reinstalled per job. (Training isn't part of the swap tool
# itself — these two lines are only here because they share this pinned-image manifest.)
SWIFT_IMAGE=modelscope-registry.cn-hangzhou.cr.aliyuncs.com/modelscope-repo/ms-swift:latest
SWIFT_IMAGE_DIGEST=

# --- Container + volume names (deterministic, so gb10-stop/audit can find them) ---
# Containers are named `swap-vllm-<served-name>` (set per-model as SERVE_CONTAINER in
# gb10-model-configs/models/<name>.env) — stable, legible in `docker ps`, and uniform across the
# swap roster. The value below is only the no-arg fallback default.
SERVE_CONTAINER=swap-vllm-qwen3.8-27b-fp8
TRAIN_CONTAINER=tokenai-train
HF_CACHE_VOL=tokenai-hf-cache          # persistent HF weight cache (docker volume)
OUT_DIR_HOST=/home/deploy/tokenai-out  # train output (adapters + merged models); mounted /out:ro in serve so merged dirs are servable by path
SERVE_PORT=8002

# --- box reachability (token-side SSH target over the LAN) ---
# Set this to your own ~/.ssh/config Host alias for the box (mDNS/LAN, not Tailscale SSH — its
# check-mode re-auth tends to hang a bare SSH alias).
GB10_SSH=your-box-ssh-alias
# curl runs ON the box (over SSH), so the alias resolves to its own hostname. Overridable so a
# driver running LOCALLY on the box (GB10_LOCAL=1, e.g. the swap-ui) can point it at localhost,
# where the bare ssh-alias name does not resolve as a hostname.
GB10_HEALTH="${GB10_HEALTH:-http://${GB10_SSH}:8002/health}"
